.TH ENGINE_PUSH 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
engine_push \- Queue s to be placed on top of the scene stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqengine.h\(dq
.BI "void engine_push(Engine *e, Scene *s);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue s to be placed on top of the scene stack. Applied after the current callback returns, so it is safe from handle_input, update, or a menu action. The scene's on_enter runs when the push is applied, not when this is called. Scenes are singletons: pushing one already on the stack shares its state.
.SH RETURN VALUE
none; a full stack (8 scenes) drops the push and logs.
.SH MODULE
core (src/engine/core/engine.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine_pop (3),
.BR engine_replace (3),
.BR engine_top (3),
.BR gge\-scenes (7),
.BR gge (1),
.BR gge\-scenes (7)
